comment0.target=ZipDownloadHandler
comment0.text=\r\n Serves "/zip?path\=..." - streams the requested folder (and everything\r\n inside it, recursively) as a single .zip file. Nothing is written to a\r\n temp file first; entries are compressed straight into the HTTP response as\r\n they're read, so this works for large folders without excess memory or disk use.\r\n
comment1.params=exchange
comment1.target=void handle(com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpExchange)
numComments=2
